 "capsule": "In the Sasanian-controlled Kushan territories of Bactria and Gandhara, a cadet line of Sasanian princes ruled with the title Kushanshah (\"king of the Kushans\"), issuing coinage that blended Sasanian and Kushan royal imagery. Under Peroz I and the rebellious Hormizd I Kushanshah (r. 277-286) this Kushano-Sasanian kingdom grew powerful enough to briefly challenge the main Sasanian court, before Shapur II reasserted direct control in campaigns of 350-358 described by Ammianus Marcellinus. Kidarite Hun invasions soon afterward ended Kushano-Sasanian rule in the region.",
